m veniam, quis nostrud exercitation ullamco laboris nisi ut aliquip ex ea commodo consequat. Duis aute irure dolor in reprehenderit in voluptate velit esse cillum dolore eu fugiat nulla pariatur. Excepteur sint occaecat cupidatat non proident, sunt in culpa qui officia deserunt mollit anim id est laborum.', 'Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit, sed do eiusmod tempor incididunt ut labore et dolore magna aliqua. Ut enim ad minim veniam, quis nostrud exercitation ullamco laboris nisi ut aliquip ex ea commodo consequat. Duis aute irure dolor in reprehenderit in voluptate velit esse cillum dolore eu fugiat nulla pariatur. Excepteur sint occaecat cupidatat non proident, sunt in culpa qui officia deserunt mollit anim id est laborum.', NULL, 'product_image_67be9cdda03dd.webp', 0, '2025-02-25 17:27:26', '2025-04-04 16:37:14', NULL),
(12, 'Augmentin Powder for Oral Suspension', 18, 47, 7, NULL, 'augmentin-powder-for-oral-suspension-250mg3125mg-for-bacterial-infections-box-of-12-sachets', 10, 'Name: Augmentin Powder for Oral Suspension 250mg/31.25mg\nType: Broad-spectrum antibiotic (beta-lactam + beta-lactamase inhibitor)\nForm: Powder for oral suspension (Box of 12 sachets)\nUse: Treats various bacterial infections (respiratory, urinary, skin, bones, etc.)', 'Active ingredients (per sachet):\n-  Amoxicillin 250mg (as amoxicillin trihydrate)\n-  Clavulanic acid 31.25mg (as potassium clavulanate)\n\nExcipients:\n-  Crospovidone, hydrated silica\n-  Flavors: peach-lemon-strawberry (includes orange, bergamot oils, etc.)\n-  Aspartame (E951), vanillin, maltodextrin, butylated hydroxyanisole (E320)\n\n', 'Used to treat infections caused by susceptible bacteria, such as:\n-  Upper respiratory infections: tonsillitis, sinusitis, otitis media\n-  Lower respiratory infections: bronchitis, pneumonia\n-  Urinary/genital infections: cystitis, pyelonephritis, gonorrhea\n-  Skin and soft tissue infections\n-  Bone and joint infections (e.g., osteomyelitis)\n-  Postpartum, intra-abdominal infections: Effective against both beta-lactamase-producing and non-producing bacteria.', 'Contraindicated in patients allergic to penicillins or cephalosporins\n\nCaution in:\n-  Liver dysfunction or history of jaundice with amoxicillin-clavulanate\n-  Renal impairment – dose adjustment needed\n-  Pregnancy and breastfeeding – use if clearly needed\n-  Patients with infectious mononucleosis – increased risk of rash\n\nMay interact with:\n-  Probenecid, allopurinol, oral contraceptives, anticoagulants, methotrexate, mycophenolate mofetil', 'Preparation: Dissolve powder in water before administration\n\nTiming: Take at the start of meals to optimize absorption and reduce GI side effects\n\nAdults:\n-  Mild/moderate infections: 1000/125mg twice/day\n-  Severe infections: 1000/125mg three times/day\n\nChildren <12 years:\n-  40–80 mg/10–20 mg per kg/day, divided into 3 doses (max 3000/375mg daily)\n\nElderly: Use adult dose unless renal impairment is present\n\nTreatment duration: Max 14 days without reassessment', 'Brand: Pharmacity\nManufacturer Address: Terras 2 Zone Industrielle de la Peyennière, 53100 Mayenne, France\nPackaging: Box of 12 sachets\nShelf Life: 24 months from manufacturing date\nStorage Conditions: Store in a tightly sealed container, in a dry place, below 30°C', NULL, 'product_image_680480d6297db.webp', 0, '2025-04-20 05:17:08', '2025-04-20 05:35:25', NULL),
(13, 'Augmentin BD 1g Film-coated Tablets', 18, 47, 11, NULL, 'augmentin-bd-1g-film-coated-tablets', 10, 'Name: Augmentin BD 1g Film-coated Tablets\nForm: Oral tablet (box of 2 blisters x 7 tablets)\nFunction: Broad-spectrum antibiotic used to treat bacterial infections\nCombination: Amoxicillin + Clavulanic acid', 'Active ingredients (per tablet):\n-  Amoxicillin 875mg (as amoxicillin trihydrate)\n-  Clavulanic acid 125mg (as potassium clavulanate)\n\nExcipients: Magnesium stearate, sodium starch glycolate, colloidal silicon dioxide, microcrystalline cellulose, titanium dioxide, HPMC 5cps & 15cps, PEG 4000 & 6000, silicone oil', 'Short-term treatment of infections in:\n-  Upper respiratory tract: tonsillitis, sinusitis, otitis media\n-  Lower respiratory tract: acute bronchitis exacerbation, lobar pneumonia, bronchopneumonia\n-  Urinary/genital tract: cystitis, urethritis, pyelonephritis\n-  Skin and soft tissue: boils, abscesses, cellulitis, infected wounds\n-  Bones and joints: osteomyelitis\n-  Dental infections: dental abscess\n-  Other infections: post-abortion infections, obstetric infections, intra-abdominal infections', 'Contraindications:\n-  Allergy to beta-lactams (penicillin, cephalosporins)\n-  History of jaundice or liver dysfunction with Augmentin\n\nUse with caution in:\n-  Renal/hepatic impairment\n-  Infectious mononucleosis\n-  Long-term therapy (risk of overgrowth of non-susceptible organisms)\n-  High-dose use (risk of crystalluria or seizures in renal dysfunction)\n-  Pregnant or breastfeeding women (only if necessary)\n\nDrug interactions:\n-  Probenecid: delays amoxicillin clearance\n-  Allopurinol: increased risk of skin rash\n-  May reduce efficacy of oral contraceptives\n-  Monitor INR if co-administered with warfarin or acenocoumarol', 'Administration:\n-  Swallow whole tablet (do not chew). Tablet may be split if necessary\n-  Take at the start of meals to improve absorption and reduce GI discomfort\n-  Do not exceed 14 days without medical review\n\nDosage (Adults & Children >12 yrs):\n-  Mild/moderate infection: 625mg twice daily\n-  Severe infection: 1g twice daily\n-  Not recommended for children ≤12 years\n\nRenal Impairment:\n-  Only use 1g tablets in patients with GFR > 30ml/min\n-  Use lower-dose formulations for GFR ≤ 30ml/min\n\nMissed dose:\n-  Take as soon as remembered unless near the next dose.\n-  Do not double the next dose\n\nOverdose management:\n-  GI upset and electrolyte imbalance may occur\n-  Hemodialysis may help remove the drug\n-  Monitor for crystalluria and renal function', 'Storage: Keep in a tightly closed container, dry place, below 30°C\n\nPackaging: Box of 2 blisters × 7 film-coated tablets\n\nShelf life: 24 months from manufacturing date\n\nBrand: GSK ETC\n\nManufacturer: SmithKline Beecham Pharmaceuticals (UK)', NULL, 'product_image_680485e62a8c8.webp', 1, '2025-04-20 05:40:41', '2025-04-20 05:40:41', NULL),
(14, ' Ciclevir 800 Glomed', 18, 47, 9, NULL, 'ciclevir-800-glomed', 15, 'Name: Ciclevir 800 Glomed Tablets\n\nForm: Oral film-coated tablet (box of 10 blisters × 5 tablets)\n\nFunction: Antiviral medication for treatment and prevention of Herpes simplex virus (HSV), chickenpox, and Herpes zoster (shingles)\n\nDrug Class: Direct-acting antiviral, nucleoside analogue reverse transcriptase inhibitor (NRTI)\n\nATC Code: J05AB01', 'Active ingredient: Aciclovir 800mg\n\nExcipients: Microcrystalline cellulose 101, sodium starch glycolate A, povidone K30, silicon dioxide, magnesium stearate', 'Treatment of HSV infections of skin and mucous membranes (including initial and recurrent genital herpes, excluding severe HSV in immunocompromised children)\n\nSuppression of recurrent HSV in immunocompetent individuals\n\nProphylaxis of HSV in immunocompromised patients\n\nTreatment of chickenpox (varicella) and shingles (Herpes zoster)', 'Contraindications:\n-  Hypersensitivity to aciclovir, valaciclovir, or any component of the formulation\n\nUse with caution in:\n-  Renal impairment: requires dosage adjustment\n-  Elderly patients: higher risk of neurotoxicity, monitor renal function\n-  Patients on high-dose aciclovir (e.g., for zoster): ensure adequate hydration to prevent crystalluria and nephrotoxicity\n-  Pregnancy: Use only when benefits outweigh risks\n-  Breastfeeding: Use with caution, though adverse effects in infants have not been reported\n-  Monitor for reduced efficacy in prolonged treatment of immunocompromised patients (possible drug resistance)', 'Administration:\n-  Oral use. Tablets may be dispersed in at least 50 ml of water if swallowing is difficult\n\nDosage:\n-  Adults:\n+  HSV infection: 200mg 5 times/day for 5 days (every 4 hours, excluding nighttime)\n+  Suppression (immunocompetent): 200mg 4x/day or 400mg 2x/day\n+  Prophylaxis (immunocompromised): 200mg 4x/day, may increase to 400mg or consider IV use\n+  Chickenpox: 800mg 5x/day for 5 days\n+  Herpes zoster: 800mg 5x/day for 7–10 days\n\n-  Children:\n+  <2 years: ½ adult dose\n+  2–5 years: 400mg 4x/day\n+  6 years: 800mg 4x/day\n+  Dosing may also be calculated as 20mg/kg (max 800mg/dose)\n\n-  Elderly & Renal Impairment:\n+  Adjust dose based on creatinine clearance\n+  Severe renal impairment: 800mg 2x/day or lower depending on infection type\n+  Ensure hydration to prevent nephrotoxicity', 'Storage: Store in a dry place, away from light, below 30°C\n\nPackaging: Box of 10 blisters × 5 tablets\n\nBrand: Abbott - Glomed\n\nManufacturer: Glomed Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd. (Vietnam)', NULL, 'product_image_68048a5d6fb07.webp', 1, '2025-04-20 05:50:40', '2025-04-20 05:50:40', NULL),
(15, 'Femara Film-Coated 2.5mg', 17, 19, 6, NULL, 'femara-film-coated-25mg', 30, 'Name: Femara Film-Coated Tablets 2.5mg\n\nForm: Oral tablet (Box of 3 blisters × 10 tablets)\n\nFunction:\n\n-  Induces ovulation (off-label use)\n\n-  Treats hormone receptor-positive breast cancer in postmenopausal women\n\nDrug Class: Aromatase inhibitor (non-steroidal)', 'Active Ingredient: Letrozole 2.5mg\n\nExcipients: Colloidal anhydrous silica, microcrystalline cellulose, lactose monohydrate, magnesium stearate, maize starch, sodium starch glycolate, hydroxypropyl methylcellulose, polyethylene glycol 8000, talc, titanium dioxide (E171), yellow iron oxide (E172)', 'Adjuvant treatment of early-stage hormone receptor-positive breast cancer in postmenopausal women\n\nExtended adjuvant treatment after prior standard adjuvant tamoxifen therapy\n\nFirst-line treatment for hormone-dependent advanced breast cancer in postmenopausal women\n\nTreatment of advanced breast cancer after failure of anti-estrogen therapy\n\nNeoadjuvant therapy in hormone receptor-positive, localized breast cancer to allow for breast-conserving surgery', 'Contraindications:\n-  Hypersensitivity to letrozole or any excipients\n-  Premenopausal women, pregnancy, breastfeeding\n\nUse with caution in:\n-  Severe hepatic impairment (Child-Pugh C): Monitor closely\n-  Renal impairment (<10 ml/min creatinine clearance): Use with caution\n-  Bone health: Risk of osteoporosis and fractures—monitor bone mineral density\n-  Driving/Operating machinery: May cause fatigue, dizziness, somnolence\n-  Women of childbearing potential: Ensure effective contraception until postmenopausal status is confirmed', 'Administration: Oral, once daily (2.5mg), with or without food\n\nDuration:\n-  Adjuvant/Extended Adjuvant: Up to 5 years or until tumor recurrence\n-  Advanced cancer: Continue until tumor progression\n\nElderly: No dose adjustment required\n\nPediatric Use: Not indicated\n\nHepatic/Renal Impairment:\n-  No dose adjustment for mild to moderate impairment\n-  Monitor closely in severe liver dysfunction', 'Storage: Do not store above 30°C. Protect from moisture\n\nPackaging: Box of 3 blisters × 10 film-coated tablets\n\nBrand: Novartis\n\nManufacturer: Switzerland', NULL, 'product_image_68048cf48f6eb.webp', 1, '2025-04-20 06:00:16', '2025-04-20 06:00:16', NULL),
(16, 'Arimidex 1mg Film-Coated', 17, 19, 6, NULL, 'arimidex-1mg-film-coated', 30, 'Name: Arimidex 1mg Film-Coated\n\nForm: Oral tablet (Box of 2 blisters × 14 tablets)\n\nFunction: Treatment of hormone receptor-positive breast cancer in postmenopausal women\n\nDrug Class: Non-steroidal aromatase inhibitor', 'Active Ingredient: Anastrozole 1mg\n\nExcipients: Lactose monohydrate, povidone, sodium starch glycolate, magnesium stearate, hypromellose, macrogol 300, titanium dioxide', 'Adjuvant treatment for early-stage estrogen receptor-positive breast cancer in postmenopausal women\n\nTreatment of advanced breast cancer in postmenopausal women (especially those who previously responded to tamoxifen)\n\nExtended adjuvant therapy after 2–3 years of prior tamoxifen treatment', 'Contraindications:\n-  Premenopausal women\n-  Pregnant or breastfeeding women\n-  Severe renal impairment (CrCl < 30 ml/min)\n-  Moderate to severe hepatic disease\n-  Hypersensitivity to anastrozole or excipients\n-  Concurrent use with tamoxifen or estrogen therapy\n\nCautions:\n-  Monitor bone mineral density regularly due to risk of osteoporosis and fractures\n-  Use bisphosphonates as needed to preserve bone health\n-  Not for use in children\n-  Use caution in galactose intolerance, Lapp lactase deficiency, or glucose-galactose malabsorption due to lactose content\n-  Monitor patients with hepatic or renal dysfunction\n-  Caution when driving or operating machinery due to fatigue or drowsiness\n\nPregnancy & Lactation:\n-  Contraindicated during pregnancy and lactation\n-  Ensure effective contraception in women of childbearing potential until postmenopausal status is confirmed', 'Dosage:\n-  Adults, including elderly: 1mg orally once daily\n-  Treatment duration: Up to 5 years for early-stage breast cancer\n-  No dose adjustment needed for mild hepatic or renal impairment\n-  Not recommended for children', 'Storage: Store below 30°C\n\nPackaging: Box of 2 blisters × 14 tablets\n\nBrand: AstraZeneca\n\nManufacturer: USA', NULL, 'product_image_68048e72da071.webp', 1, '2025-04-20 06:06:39', '2025-04-20 06:06:39', NULL),
(17, 'Xatral XL 10mg Prolonged-Release', 16, 45, 8, NULL, 'xatral-xl-10mg-prolonged-release', 25, 'Name: Xatral XL 10mg Prolonged-Release Tablets\n\nForm: Oral tablet, extended-release (Box of 1 blister × 30 tablets)\n\nFunction: Treatment of urinary symptoms associated with benign prostatic hyperplasia (BPH)\n\nDrug Class: Alpha-1 adrenergic receptor antagonist', 'Active Ingredient: Alfuzosin hydrochloride 10mg\n\nExcipients: (Not explicitly listed; refer to packaging if needed)', 'Treatment of functional symptoms of BPH in men\n\nAdjunct therapy for acute urinary retention related to BPH (used with catheterization)', 'Contraindications:\n-  Hypersensitivity to alfuzosin or excipients\n-  Orthostatic hypotension\n-  Severe hepatic or renal impairment\n-  Co-administration with ritonavir\n\nWarnings and Cautions:\n-  Risk of orthostatic hypotension—monitor especially after first dose\n-  Intraoperative Floppy Iris Syndrome (IFIS) in cataract surgery patients—inform ophthalmologist if using or used alfuzosin\n-  Use with caution in elderly or patients on other alpha-blockers\n-  Alfuzosin may exacerbate angina—stop if angina worsens\n-  Do not crush, chew, or break the tablet (prolonged-release formulation)\n-  Avoid in patients with lactose intolerance or absorption issues (if excipient includes lactose)\n\nDriving & Machinery:\n-  May cause dizziness, fatigue, or visual disturbances—caution required\n\nPregnancy & Breastfeeding:\n-  Not indicated for women—consult a physician if exposed\n\n', 'Administration:\n-  Take once daily after dinner, with a full glass of water\n-  Swallow whole—do not break or crush\n\nSpecial Instruction with Catheterization:\n-  Start alfuzosin on the day of catheter insertion\n-  Continue for 3–4 days total (including 1 day post-catheter removal)\n\nMissed Dose:\n-  Do not double dose—take the next dose at the regular time\n\nOverdose Management:\n-  Lay patient flat; manage hypotension supportively\n-  Hemodialysis unlikely to be effective due to high protein binding', 'Storage: Store below 30°C, in a dry place away from light\n\nPackaging: Box containing 1 blister × 30 extended-release tablets\n\nBrand: (Manufacturer details can be found on product packaging)', NULL, 'product_image_680490023df28.webp', 1, '2025-04-20 06:14:03', '2025-04-20 06:14:03', NULL),
(18, 'Floezy 0.4mg Prolonged-Release', 16, 6, 8, NULL, 'floezy-04mg-prolonged-release', 35, 'Name: Floezy 0.4mg Prolonged-Release Tablets\n\nForm: Oral prolonged-release tablet (Box of 3 blisters × 10 tablets)\n\nFunction: Symptomatic treatment of lower urinary tract symptoms (LUTS) associated with benign prostatic hyperplasia (BPH)\n\nDrug Class: Alpha-1 adrenergic receptor antagonist', 'Active Ingredient: Tamsulosin hydrochloride 0.4 mg (equivalent to 0.367 mg tamsulosin)\n\nExcipients: Hypromellose, microcrystalline cellulose, carbomer, colloidal anhydrous silica, red iron oxide, magnesium stearate, purified water', 'Treatment of lower urinary tract symptoms (LUTS) associated with benign prostatic hyperplasia (BPH)', 'Contraindications:\n-  Hypersensitivity to tamsulosin or excipients\n-  History of orthostatic hypotension\n-  Severe hepatic impairment\n\nCautions:\n-  Orthostatic hypotension may occur; advise patients to lie/sit down if dizzy\n-  Rule out other causes of LUTS before initiating treatment (e.g., via digital rectal exam, PSA test)\n-  Caution in severe renal impairment (CrCl < 10 ml/min)\n-  Intraoperative Floppy Iris Syndrome (IFIS) may occur in cataract surgery patients — inform surgeon\n-  Not recommended for use in women or children\n\nPregnancy & Lactation:\n-  Not indicated for use in women\n\nDriving & Machinery:\n-  Caution advised due to possible dizziness or faintness', 'Dosage:\n-  1 tablet (0.4mg) once daily\n-  Can be taken with or without food\n\nAdministration:\n-  Swallow whole with water; do not chew or crush\n\nMissed Dose:\n-  Do not double the dose. Take the next dose as scheduled', 'Storage: Store below 30°C, in a dry place, protected from moisture and light\n\nPackaging: Box of 3 blisters × 10 prolonged-release tablets\n\nBrand: Mega Lifesciences\n\nManufacturer: Synthon Hispania Sl. (Spain)', NULL, 'product_image_6804917226da4.webp', 1, '2025-04-20 06:20:00', '2025-04-20 06:20:00', NULL),
(19, 'Daygra 100mg Film-Coated', 12, 2, 8, NULL, 'daygra-100mg-film-coated', 20, 'Name: Daygra 100mg Film-Coated Tablets\n\nForm: Oral tablet (Box of 1 blister × 4 film-coated tablets)\n\nFunction: Treatment of erectile dysfunction (ED) in men\n\nDrug Class: Phosphodiesterase type 5 (PDE5) inhibitor', 'Active Ingredient: Sildenafil 100 mg (as Sildenafil citrate)\n\nExcipients: Microcrystalline cellulose (101, 102), crospovidone, mannitol, colloidal silicon dioxide, magnesium stearate, opadry white, opadry red, sunset yellow lake, opadry silver', 'Treatment of erectile dysfunction in men — the inability to achieve or maintain an erection sufficient for satisfactory sexual performance.', 'Contraindications:\n-   Hypersensitivity to sildenafil or any component\n-   Concurrent use of nitrates or nitric oxide donors\n-   Severe liver impairment\n-   Recent stroke or myocardial infarction\n-   Unstable angina, severe heart failure\n-   Retinal disorders such as retinitis pigmentosa\n\nCautions:\n-   Assess cardiovascular status before prescribing (sexual activity may pose a risk)\n-   Use cautiously in patients with severe renal or hepatic impairment\n-   Caution in patients with anatomical deformities of the penis or predisposing conditions for priapism\n-   Not recommended for those with high cardiac risk during sexual activity\n-   Avoid combining sildenafil with other erectile dysfunction treatments\n-   Not for pediatric use\n\nDriving & Machinery:\n-   Avoid if experiencing dizziness or visual disturbances', 'Adults:\n-   Recommended dose: 50mg about 1 hour before sexual activity\n-   May adjust to 100mg (max) or 25mg depending on efficacy/tolerance\n\nElderly (>65 years):\n-   Start with 25mg\n\nRenal/hepatic impairment:\n-   Start with 25mg\n\nConcomitant medication considerations:\n-   Use ≤25mg with CYP3A4 inhibitors\n-   Do not exceed 25mg every 48 hours with ritonavir\n-   Use with alpha-blockers cautiously — spacing at least 4 hours', 'Storage: Store in a dry place, protected from light, at temperature not exceeding 30°C\n\nPackaging: Box of 1 blister × 4 film-coated tablets\n\nBrand: Glomed\n\nManufacturer: Glomed Pharmaceutical Joint Stock Company (Vietnam)', NULL, 'product_image_68049d776e60a.webp', 1, '2025-04-20 07:12:13', '2025-04-20 07:12:13', NULL),
(20, 'Casilas 20mg', 12, 2, 8, NULL, 'casilas-20mg', 35, 'Name: Casilas 20mg\n\nForm: Film-coated tablet\n\nFunction: Treatment of erectile dysfunction (ED) in adult men\n\nDosage form & packaging: 2 blisters × 2 film-coated tablets per box\n\nDrug class: PDE5 inhibitor\n\nManufacturer: Davipharm (Việt Nam)', 'Active ingredient: Tadalafil 20mg\n\nExcipients: Microcrystalline cellulose MI 01, betacyclodextrin, maize starch, povidone, magnesium stearate, croscarmellose sodium, silicon dioxide, HPMC E6, titanium dioxide, talc, PEG 4000, polysorbate 80, castor oil, yellow iron oxide', 'Treatment of erectile dysfunction in adult men\n\nNote: Effective only in presence of sexual stimulation', 'Cardiovascular Risk: Evaluate cardiovascular status before prescribing due to risks from sexual activity\n\nPriapism Risk: Medical attention needed if erection persists >4 hours\n\nLiver/Kidney:\n-  Not recommended for severe hepatic/renal impairment\n-  No dose adjustment required for mild/moderate cases\n\nDrug Interactions: Use caution when co-administered with CYP3A4 inhibitors\n\nUse in Special Populations:\n-  Elderly: No dose adjustment needed\n-  Children: Not indicated\n-  Diabetes patients: No dose adjustment needed', 'Route: Oral, with or without food\n\nTiming: ~30 minutes before sexual activity\n\nFrequency: Max 1 dose/day\n\nNot for continuous daily use, unless directed by a physician', 'Storage: Below 30°C, dry place, away from light and children\n\nPackaging: Yellow pear-shaped film-coated tablet, both sides plain\n\nBrand: Casilas\n\nManufacturer: Công ty CP Dược phẩm Đạt Vi Phú (Davipharm)', NULL, 'product_image_68049f4275585.webp', 1, '2025-04-20 07:19:56', '2025-04-20 07:19:56', NULL),
(21, 'Combigan Eye Drops 5ml', 10, 47, 11, NULL, 'combigan-eye-drops-5ml', 10, 'Combigan is an ophthalmic solution produced by Allergan Pharmaceuticals Ireland, combining two active substances: brimonidine tartrate 2.0 mg/mL and timolol maleate 6.8 mg/mL (equivalent to 5 mg timolol). It is indicated for reducing intraocular pressure (IOP) in patients with chronic open-angle glaucoma or ocular hypertension who are insufficiently responsive to topical beta-blockers alone.', 'Active ingredients:\n-  Brimonidine tartrate: 2 mg/mL\n-  Timolol maleate: equivalent to 5 mg/mL of timolol\n\nExcipients: Benzalkonium chloride, sodium phosphate monobasic monohydrate, sodium phosphate dibasic heptahydrate, hydrochloric acid or sodium hydroxide (for pH adjustment), purified water.', 'Reduction of elevated intraocular pressure in patients with chronic open-angle glaucoma or ocular hypertension who are inadequately responsive to topical beta-blockers.', 'Contraindicated in patients with bronchial asthma, severe chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, sinus bradycardia, AV block (second or third degree), overt cardiac failure, or cardiogenic shock.\n\nNot to be used in infants and children under 2 years old.\n\nContraindicated in patients on monoamine oxidase inhibitors (MAOIs) or tricyclic antidepressants.\n\nCaution is advised in patients with cardiovascular disease, diabetes, hyperthyroidism, myasthenia gravis, corneal diseases, and those undergoing surgery.\n\nBenzalkonium chloride can discolor soft contact lenses – remove lenses prior to administration and wait 15 minutes before reinserting.\n\nMay impair driving and machine operation due to side effects like drowsiness, blurred vision, or visual disturbances.\n\nNot recommended during pregnancy or lactation unless clearly needed. Monitor neonates if used during pregnancy.\n\nNot recommended in pediatric use due to high incidence of somnolence in children under 7 years.', 'Dosage: One drop in the affected eye(s) twice daily, approximately 12 hours apart.\n\nAdministration: Instill directly into the conjunctival sac. Occlude the nasolacrimal duct for 1 minute to reduce systemic absorption.\n\nMissed dose: Use as soon as remembered unless it\'s near the next dose. Do not double dose.\n\nOverdose: Supportive and symptomatic treatment recommended. Monitor for systemic beta-blocker or alpha-agonist side effects.', 'Brand: Allergan\n\nManufacturer: Allergan Pharmaceuticals Ireland\n\nPackaging: 1 bottle x 5mL\n\nStorage: Store below 30°C, protect from light, keep in original carton.', NULL, 'product_image_6804a1ffd3fa6.webp', 1, '2025-04-20 07:29:15', '2025-04-20 07:29:15', NULL),
(22, 'Ciloxan 0.3% Eye Drops', 10, 19, 11, NULL, 'ciloxan-03-eye-drops', 15, 'Ciloxan 0.3% is a sterile ophthalmic solution containing ciprofloxacin, a broad-spectrum fluoroquinolone antibiotic, used to treat bacterial infections of the eye. Each bottle contains 5 mL of solution for topical ocular use.', 'Active Ingredient: Ciprofloxacin hydrochloride equivalent to 3 mg ciprofloxacin per mL\n\nPreservative: Benzalkonium chloride 0.006%\n\nExcipients: Sodium acetate, mannitol, acetic acid, disodium edetate, hydrochloric acid and/or sodium hydroxide (to adjust pH), and purified water', 'Ciloxan is indicated for the treatment of ocular infections caused by susceptible strains of bacteria in the following conditions:\n\n-  Corneal ulcers:\n+  Pseudomonas aeruginosa, Serratia marcescens, Staphylococcus aureus, Staphylococcus epidermidis, Streptococcus pneumoniae, Streptococcus (viridans group)\n\n-  Bacterial conjunctivitis:\n+  Staphylococcus aureus, Staphylococcus epidermidis, Streptococcus pneumoniae\n\n', 'Prolonged use may result in overgrowth of non-susceptible organisms, including fungi. If superinfection occurs, appropriate therapy should be initiated.\n\nDiscontinue use immediately upon signs of hypersensitivity or skin rash.\n\nWhite crystalline precipitates have been reported in 16.6% of patients with corneal ulcers, usually resolving spontaneously without affecting clinical outcomes.\n\nAvoid contact of the dropper tip with any surface to prevent contamination.\n\nUse in Pregnancy: Only use if the potential benefit justifies the potential risk to the fetus.\n\nUse in Lactation: Caution is advised. Systemic ciprofloxacin has been detected in breast milk.\n\nDriving & Machine Operation: Temporary blurred vision may impair the ability to drive or operate machinery. Wait until vision clears.', 'Route: Ophthalmic (topical to the eye)\n\nCorneal Ulcer Treatment:\n-  Day 1: 2 drops every 15 minutes for the first 6 hours, then every 30 minutes for the remainder of the day.\n-  Day 2: 2 drops every hour.\n-  Days 3–14: 2 drops every 4 hours.\n-  Treatment may extend beyond 14 days if epithelial regeneration is incomplete; re-evaluation by a physician is recommended.\n\nBacterial Conjunctivitis Treatment:\n-  Days 1–2: 1–2 drops every 2 hours while awake\n-  Days 3–7: 1–2 drops every 4 hours while awake\n-  Maximum duration: 21 days\n\nPediatric Use: Safety not established for children under 1 year. Children ≥1 year may use adult dosage.\n\n', 'Brand: Alcon\n\nManufacturer: SA Alcon-Couvreur NV\n\nCountry of Manufacture: Belgium\n\nStorage: Store at 2°C to 30°C. Protect from light.\n\nPackaging: 1 bottle × 5 mL', NULL, 'product_image_6804a2cf4be03.webp', 1, '2025-04-20 07:33:10', '2025-04-20 07:33:10', NULL),
(23, 'Vitamin B1 50mg Mekophar', 9, 1, 9, NULL, 'vitamin-b1-50mg-mekophar', 40, 'Vitamin B1 50mg is a pharmaceutical product manufactured by Mekophar Chemical Pharmaceutical Joint-Stock Company (Mekophar). It is formulated as oral tablets containing thiamine (vitamin B1), used to treat vitamin B1 deficiency. The tablets are green, round, with \"VITAMIN B1\" engraved on one side and \"50\" on the other. Packaging includes bottles of 100 or 200 tablets.', 'Active Ingredient: Thiamine mononitrate (Vitamin B1) 50mg\n\nExcipients: Blue patente color, tapioca starch, corn starch, lactose, magnesium stearate (qs for 1 tablet)', 'Indicated for the treatment of vitamin B1 deficiency, including:\n-  Mild chronic deficiency\n-  Severe deficiency requiring higher dosing\n\n', 'Contraindications:\n-  Hypersensitivity to any component of the product\n\nWarnings and precautions:\n-  Caution in individuals with a history of allergy to vitamin B1.\n-  Contains lactose – use caution in patients with rare hereditary conditions such as galactose intolerance, Lapp lactase deficiency, or glucose-galactose malabsorption.\n-  Not recommended for pregnant or breastfeeding women.\n\nUse in Children:\n-  Not recommended for children under 3 years old.\n\nDriving and Machine Operation:\n-  No known effects on the ability to drive or operate machinery.', 'Route of Administration: Oral\n\nDosage:\n-  Adults, elderly, and children ≥ 3 years old:\n+  Mild deficiency: 1 tablet/day\n+  Severe deficiency: 2 tablets, 3 times/day\n-  Children < 3 years old: Not recommended\n\nMissed dose: Take as soon as remembered, skip if near the next dose. Do not double the dose.\n\nOverdose: No reported overdose cases. In case of suspected overdose, discontinue use and provide symptomatic and supportive treatment.', 'Manufacturer: Mekophar Chemical Pharmaceutical Joint-Stock Company (Mekophar)\n\nCountry of Origin: Vietnam\n\nPackaging: Bottle of 100 tablets\n\nStorage: Store in a dry place, away from light, at temperature not exceeding 30°C.', NULL, 'product_image_6804a3e8bcbbd.webp', 1, '2025-04-20 07:38:32', '2025-04-20 07:38:32', NULL),
(24, 'Scanneuron Stella Tablet', 9, 2, 9, NULL, 'scanneuron-stella-tablet', 25, 'Scanneuron is a pharmaceutical product manufactured by Stella, containing a high-dose combination of neurotropic vitamins. It is indicated as supportive therapy for neurological disorders such as neuralgia, peripheral neuritis, optic neuritis, neuropathy caused by diabetes or alcohol, polyneuritis, paresthesia, sciatica, and convulsions caused by central nervous system hyperexcitability.', 'Vitamin B1 (Thiamine nitrate): 100 mg\n\nVitamin B6 (Pyridoxine hydrochloride): 200 mg\n\nVitamin B12 (Cyanocobalamin): 200 mcg', 'Scanneuron is indicated for the supportive treatment of:\n-  Neuralgia\n-  Peripheral neuritis\n-  Optic neuritis\n-  Diabetic and alcoholic neuropathy\n-  Polyneuritis\n-  Paresthesia\n-  Sciatica\n-  Convulsions due to increased CNS excitability', 'Contraindicated in individuals with hypersensitivity to vitamin B1, B6, B12, or any excipients.\n\nContraindicated in patients with malignant tumors due to vitamin B12\'s role in promoting rapidly growing tissues.\n\nNot recommended for individuals with allergic conditions (asthma, eczema).\n\nLong-term use of high-dose vitamin B6 (200 mg/day for over 30 days) may cause sensory neuropathy or vitamin B6 dependency.\n\nShould not be used without diagnosis in suspected vitamin B12 deficiency cases.\n\nUse cautiously in pregnant and breastfeeding women.\n\nThe safety and effectiveness in children have not been established.', 'Dosage: 1 tablet per day or as prescribed by a physician.\n\nRoute: Oral\n\nOverdose: High doses of vitamin B6 (2–7 g/day or >200 mg/day for over two months) may lead to sensory neuropathy, which usually resolves within six months of discontinuation.\n\nMissed dose: Take as soon as remembered unless near the next dose—do not double the dose.', 'Packaging: Box of 10 blisters x 10 tablets\n\nManufacturer: Stella\n\nCountry of origin: Vietnam\n\nStorage: Store in a cool, dry place away from direct sunlight and out of reach of children.', NULL, 'product_image_6804a4f453ae2.webp', 1, '2025-04-20 07:42:02', '2025-04-20 07:42:02', NULL),
(25, 'Gentriboston Topical Cream 10g', 1, 5, 9, NULL, 'gentriboston-topical-cream-10g', 10, 'Gentriboston is a topical medication produced by Boston Pharmaceutical Joint Stock Company (Vietnam), formulated with a combination of clotrimazole, betamethasone dipropionate, and gentamicin. It is used to treat inflammatory skin conditions responsive to corticosteroids, fungal skin infections, and secondary bacterial infections. The product is available in the form of a cream in a 10g tube.', 'Active Ingredients (per 10g tube):\n-  Clotrimazole 100 mg\n-  Betamethasone dipropionate 6.4 mg\n-  Gentamicin (as gentamicin sulfate) 10,000 IU\n\nFunction:\n-  Clotrimazole: Antifungal\n-  Betamethasone dipropionate: Potent corticosteroid with anti-inflammatory effects\n-  Gentamicin: Broad-spectrum antibiotic', 'Inflammatory skin disorders responsive to corticosteroids, including eczema, contact dermatitis, diaper rash, psoriasis, and pruritus\n\nDermatitis with secondary bacterial infection\n\nFungal infections of the feet, body, scalp, and groin associated with inflammation and bacterial superinfection', 'Avoid use in patients with hypersensitivity to corticosteroids, aminoglycosides, or any component of the cream\n\nDo not use in patients with diabetes, psychosis, systemic fungal infections, or viral infections of the skin\n\nUse caution when applying over large areas, on broken skin, or under occlusion\n\nNot recommended for children under 2 years old\n\nUse with caution in children and on sensitive areas (face, genitals, intertriginous areas)\n\nProlonged use may suppress the hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal (HPA) axis and cause systemic effects\n\nAvoid contact with eyes and mucous membranes\n\nUse during pregnancy or breastfeeding only if the potential benefit justifies the potential risk\n\nGentamicin applied topically can cause ototoxicity and nephrotoxicity if absorbed systemically', 'For topical use only\n\nAdults and children over 12 years: Apply a thin layer to the affected area twice daily (morning and evening)\n\nChildren 2–12 years: Use a small amount and apply no more than twice daily with at least 6–12 hours between applications\n\nTreatment duration depends on clinical response but should not exceed 2–4 weeks for fungal infections (e.g., athlete’s foot)\n\nFor use on the face or sensitive areas, limit treatment to 5–7 days and only under medical supervision\n\nWash hands before and after application', 'Brand: Embryolisse\n\nManufacturer: Boston Pharmaceutical Joint Stock Company\n\nCountry of Manufacture: Vietnam\n\nPackaging: Box of 1 tube x 10g\n\nStorage Conditions: Store in a dry, cool place below 30°C. Protect from light and moisture.', NULL, 'product_image_6804a64b2ce70.webp', 1, '2025-04-20 07:47:58', '2025-04-20 07:47:58', NULL),
(26, 'Betamethasone Topical Gel 30g', 1, 7, 9, NULL, 'betamethasone-topical-gel-30g', 15, 'Betamethasone is a potent corticosteroid used for the treatment of various inflammatory and allergic skin conditions. It helps reduce swelling, itching, and redness associated with skin issues. It may also be used in managing certain musculoskeletal, ocular, and respiratory disorders when indicated.', 'Active ingredient: Betamethasone dipropionate 19.2mg\n\nExcipients: Not specified in detail', 'Betamethasone is indicated for the treatment of:\n-  Musculoskeletal disorders: psoriatic arthritis, rheumatoid arthritis, ankylosing spondylitis, synovitis, gout.\n-  Dermatological conditions: bullous dermatitis, Stevens-Johnson syndrome, exfoliative dermatitis, severe psoriasis, eczema, urticaria.\n-  Chronic allergic conditions: seasonal allergic rhinitis, nasal polyps, asthma, atopic dermatitis, drug allergies.\n-  Ocular conditions: allergic conjunctivitis, keratitis, corneal ulcers, ophthalmic herpes zoster, iritis, retinitis, optic neuritis.\n-  Respiratory conditions: Loeffler’s syndrome, beryllium poisoning, acute pulmonary tuberculosis, pneumothorax, pulmonary fibrosis.', 'Do not use in individuals hypersensitive to any components of the formulation.\n\nContraindicated in perioral dermatitis, acne vulgaris, or rosacea.\n\nAvoid in patients with uncontrolled systemic infections, including viral, fungal, or bacterial.\n\nNot suitable for patients with latent or active tuberculosis, or those with diabetes or peptic ulcer disease without proper supervision.\n\nNot for ophthalmic use or for infants under 1 month of age.\n\nLong-term use may result in cataracts, glaucoma, secondary eye infections, fluid and electrolyte imbalance, and adrenal suppression.\n\nDiscontinue slowly to avoid secondary adrenal insufficiency.\n\nUse cautiously in herpes infections, pregnant or breastfeeding women.', 'Route: Topical (external use only)\n\nDosage:\n-  Initial: 0.25g to 8g/day depending on severity.\n-  Children (6–12 years): 17.5g to 20g depending on body weight, with close supervision.\n-  Joint inflammation: 1g to 2.5g/day for 5–7 days.\n-  Asthma: 3.5g to 4.5g/day initially, then reduce to 0.25g–0.5g/day for maintenance.\n-  Allergic rhinitis: 1.5g to 2.5g on day 1, reduce to 0.5g/day.\n-  Maximum daily dose should not exceed 45g.\n\nAlways consult a physician before use.\n', 'Manufacturer: Medipharco-Tenamyd\n\nProduction Site: Medipharco Pharmaceutical Joint Stock Company, Vietnam\n\nPackaging: Box of 1 tube x 30g\n\nStorage: Store between 20°C and 30°C, in original packaging, away from direct sunlight. Do not freeze.', NULL, 'product_image_6804a7619177a.webp', 1, '2025-04-20 07:52:46', '2025-04-20 07:52:46', NULL);
